1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
一个国家欠债太多，会动你的存款吗？
Can too much national debt touch your savings?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
通常不会直接没收，但会换一种方式。
Usually not by confiscation, but by another route.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
钱不会凭空消失，只会换一个人付。
Money does not vanish. Someone else pays.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
账单不会消失，只会往下传。
The bill never disappears. It gets passed down.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
国债的账单：国家欠债，最后谁买单？
The Debt Bill

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
先看三张账单：政府、银行、家庭。
Three bills: government, banks, households.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
政府的利息、银行的资本、你的购买力。
Government interest, bank capital, your purchasing power.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
三张账单，一张比一张更靠近你。
Three bills, each closer to you.

9
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
第一张：政府的账单。
Bill one: the government.

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
政府借钱修路、发工资、救经济，
Governments borrow to build, pay, and rescue.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
但借来的钱，要付利息。
But borrowed money carries interest.

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
债务越大，利息越重。
The bigger the debt, the heavier the interest.

13
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
利息不创造新东西，只挪走教育医疗。
Interest creates nothing; it moves school and hospital money.

14
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
预算被利息挤瘦，公共服务先排队。
Interest squeezes the budget; public services queue.

15
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
利息，是预算里最硬的一笔。
Interest is the hardest line in the budget.

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
第二张：银行的账单。
Bill two: the banks.

17
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
银行爱买国债，安全、能抵押。
Banks love government bonds: safe and pledgeable.

18
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
国债一跌价，银行资本就有窟窿。
When bonds fall, bank capital gets a hole.

19
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
存款人一慌，挤兑就来了。
When depositors panic, a run begins.

20
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,000
银行卖资产，政府再来救。
Banks sell assets; the state steps in.

21
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
政府救银行，债务又回到政府。
The rescue returns the debt to the state.

22
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
这是主权—银行循环。
The sovereign-bank loop.

23
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:32,000
第三张：你家的账单。
Bill three: your household.

24
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,000
先来的不是没收，是通胀。
It starts with inflation, not confiscation.

25
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
同样一百块，买到的东西变少。
The same hundred yuan buys less.

26
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
工资追不上物价，存款在变薄。
Wages lag prices; savings thin out.

27
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,000
利率一升，房贷和消费贷更贵。
Higher rates make mortgages and loans dearer.

28
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
存款还在，购买力先没了。
Savings remain. Purchasing power goes first.

29
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
但有两种债，结局完全不同。
But two kinds of debt end very differently.

30
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,000
借自己的货币，还是借别人的货币？
Borrow in your own currency, or someone else’s?

31
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,000
本币债，政府不会名义上还不起。
In local currency, the state need not default nominally.

32
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
它可以用通胀和贬值，把债稀释掉。
It can inflate and devalue the debt away.

33
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:12,000
外币债，政府真的可能没有美元。
In foreign currency, the state can run out of dollars.

34
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
还不上，就是违约、重组、进口崩溃。
Then comes default, restructuring, and import collapse.

35
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,000
阿根廷、黎巴嫩、斯里兰卡，都走过。
Argentina, Lebanon, and Sri Lanka have been there.

36
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,000
极端时，银行会限取、冻结、强制换币。
In extremes: withdrawal limits, freezes, forced conversion.

37
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:32,000
账单（Sovereign Debt）
主权债务

38
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,000
国家欠债，先被重新定价的是货币。
National debt reprices the currency first.

39
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:40,000
最后才是存款、工资和选择权。
Savings, wages, and choices come after.

40
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
这张账单，最后落在每个拿钱的人手里。
The bill lands with everyone holding money.

41
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:00,000
下一次，先看你的购买力。
Next time, look at your purchasing power first.
